  "query_preview": "..The main story across the Southwest continues to be\nan area of high pressure dominating the region. This pattern will\nbring mild temperatures, dry conditions, and light winds through\nThursday. The weather story will begin to shift on Friday as a\ncouple of disturbances begin to move towards Arizona. The first\nshortwave looks to pass along the Arizona/Mexico border, keeping\nprecipitation chances focused across the southern portion of our\nCWA. Following quickly behind, a larger trough will push down from\nthe Pacific Northwest. Heaviest precipitation looks to be on\nSaturday, but overall rainfall accumulation are forecast to be\nroughly 0.5\" or less. However, a few localized areas near upslope\nlocation may see up to 0.75\". Late Saturday into Sunday we could \nsee a few flurries mix down towards 7000-7500', but otherwise snow\nlevels are anticipated to remain above 8000-8500'. \n\nSunday and Monday a brief ridge pattern will build across the\nSouthwest. This will allow temperatures to quickly warm and\ndry/calm conditions to return to the forecast. More unsettled \nweather looks to pass through on Tuesday, but confidence is still \nlow at this time on exact details.",
